---
import BootMenu from '../BootMenu.astro';
import Callout from '../Callout.astro';
---

<div
  style="display: flex; flex-direction: column; gap: 28px; padding: 40px 0 56px"
>
  <div style="display: flex; align-items: center; gap: 12px">
    <div
      style="width: 12px; height: 18px; background: var(--color-7dffa8); box-shadow: 0 0 8px var(--color-7dffa8)"
    >
    </div>
    <div class="num">A practical guide for non-engineers</div>
  </div>
  <h1 style="font-size: clamp(40px, 8.5vw, 64px); line-height: 1">
    <span class="hero">Getting going with AI</span>
  </h1>
  <p class="lede">
    From "I chat with Claude sometimes" to "Claude builds small things on my
    computer while I check its work".
  </p>
  <div
    class="card"
    style="display: flex; flex-direction: column; gap: 12px; border-color: var(--color-2a6b42)"
  >
    <div class="num" style="color: var(--color-b8ffd0)">For the reader</div>
    <p>
      By the end, you will have a one-page website of your photos, working on
      your computer. Claude chat helps write the request; Claude Code builds it.
      You decide what changes and check the result.
    </p>
  </div>

  <div class="card workflow">
    <div class="num" id="workflow-title">The whole workflow</div>
    <ol aria-labelledby="workflow-title">
      <li><strong>Claude chat</strong>{' '}<span>writes the request</span></li>
      <li><strong>Claude Code</strong>{' '}<span>proposes changes</span></li>
      <li>
        <strong>You approve</strong>{' '}<span
          >then Claude Code makes changes</span
        >
      </li>
      <li><strong>Browser</strong>{' '}<span>you inspect the result</span></li>
    </ol>
    <p>
      Here, approval means you have reviewed the plan and told the agent to
      proceed, not that you approve every edit separately. Asking an agent to
      wait is an instruction, not a technical lock.
    </p>
  </div>
  <Callout title={'Before you start'} warning
    ><svg
      slot="icon"
      width="22"
      height="22"
      viewBox="0 0 24 24"
      fill="none"
      stroke="var(--color-ffb347)"
      stroke-width="2"
      stroke-linecap="round"
      stroke-linejoin="round"
      ><path d="M12 9v4"></path><path d="M12 17h.01"></path><path
        d="M10.3 3.9 1.8 18a2 2 0 0 0 1.7 3h17a2 2 0 0 0 1.7-3L13.7 3.9a2 2 0 0 0-3.4 0z"
      ></path></svg
    ><p>
      Use copies, keep private files out, and keep backups outside the agent's
      working project. Read the <a href="#s2">four safety rules</a> before starting.
      These tools change fast; check the live docs:
      <a href="https://code.claude.com/docs/en/setup">Claude Code</a> and
      <a href="https://delta.dev/docs">Delta</a>. If a step does not match your
      screen, do not guess. Send me the error text, with private details
      removed.
    </p></Callout
  >
  <p>
    Product guidance last checked against Claude Code and Delta docs on
    <time datetime="2026-09-27">27 September 2026</time>.
  </p>
  <div style="display: flex; flex-direction: column; gap: 10px">
    <div class="num">What is in here</div>
    <BootMenu />
  </div>
</div>

<style>
  .workflow ol {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: repeat(4, minmax(0, 1fr));
    gap: 24px;
    list-style: none;
    padding: 0;
    margin: 20px 0;
  }

  .workflow li {
    position: relative;
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    gap: 8px;
  }

  .workflow li:not(:last-child)::after {
    content: '→';
    position: absolute;
    right: -20px;
    top: 0;
    color: var(--color-7dffa8);
  }

  .workflow strong {
    color: var(--color-b8ffd0);
  }

  @media (max-width: 600px) {
    .workflow ol {
      grid-template-columns: 1fr;
      gap: 32px;
    }

    .workflow li:not(:last-child)::after {
      content: '↓';
      top: auto;
      right: auto;
      bottom: -28px;
    }
  }
</style>
